FIRST QUARTER 2020 FINANCIAL RESULTS.Q1 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.44.Q1 REVENUE $405.1 MILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $358 MILLION.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.15 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q1 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.21.TEMPORARILY SUSPENDING ITS 2020 GUIDANCE.AS OF MARCH 31, 2020, CO HELD $1.5 BILLION IN CASH AND MARKETABLE SECURITIES AND CO'S REVOLVING CREDIT FACILITY REMAINS UNDRAWN."}{'symbol': 'F', 'date': '2020-04-29 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': "Ford Says It Believes Phased Restart Of Co's Manufacturing Plants, Supply Network Is Probable Commencing In Q2 2020", 'text': "FORD MOTOR - BELIEVE PHASED RESTART OF CO'S MANUFACTURING PLANTS, SUPPLY NETWORK & OTHER DEPENDENT FUNCTIONS IS PROBABLE OF COMMENCING IN Q2 2020.FORD - ALTHOUGH ULTIMATE IMPACT ON CO FROM COVID-19 CANNOT BE DETERMINED AT THIS TIME, CO EXPECTS FY 2020 RESULTS OF OPERATIONS TO BE ADVERSELY AFFECTED.FORD - BELIEVE PHASED RESTART, CASH ON HAND, FUNDS RECEIVED IN APRIL 2020 WILL PROVIDE SUFFICIENT LIQUIDITY TO FUND OPERATIONS FOR AT LEAST NEXT 12 MONTHS.FORD - EXPECT GOVERNMENT RELIEF PROGRAMS, FORD CREDIT’S DEFERRAL PROGRAMS, AMONG OTHERS TO MITIGATE IMPACTS, BUT RESULT IN CREDIT LOSSES EXPECTED TO BE ADVERSE.FORD - ESTIMATE TO INCUR CHARGES IN 2020 OF $700 MILLION - $1.2 BILLION RELATED TO ACTIONS, ATTRIBUTABLE TO EMPLOYEE SEPARATIONS, DEPRECIATION, SOME  SETTLEMENTS.FORD - AGGREGATE RISK ESTIMATE FOR REASONABLY POSSIBLE LOSS IN EXCESS OF ACCRUALS FOR ALL MATERIAL MATTERS TO BE A RANGE OF UP TO ABOUT $400 MILLION.FORD - WE HAVE REASONABLY POSSIBLE RISK OF LOSS FOR AN EMISSION CERTIFICATION MATTER.FORD - AT THIS STAGE, CANNOT ESTIMATE RISK OF LOSS OR PREDICT THE OUTCOME OF EMISSION CERTIFICATE MATTER.FORD - IN TOTAL, THE IMPACT OF COVID-19 DETERIORATED FIRST QUARTER 2020 EBT BY ABOUT $700 MILLION.FORD - FOR 2020, FORD CREDIT NOW PROJECTS FULL YEAR PUBLIC TERM FUNDING IN THE RANGE OF $12 BILLION TO $22 BILLION."}{'symbol': 'F', 'date': '2020-04-29 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Ford Says It Is Delaying Start Of Autonomous Vehicle Commercial Services To 2022', 'text': 'FORD MOTOR CO - QUARTER-END CASH BALANCE OF $34.3 BILLION; LIQUIDITY OF $35.1 BILLION.FORD MOTOR CO - IN NORTH AMERICA, Q1 WHOLESALE UNITS DOWN 18%, REFLECTING PRIMARILY COVID-19 RELATED DISRUPTION.FORD MOTOR CO - IN MOBILITY, START OF AV COMMERCIAL SERVICES MOVED TO 2022.FORD MOTOR CO -  REMAIN COMMITTED TO A STRONG BALANCE SHEET.FORD MOTOR SAYS FOR FORD CREDIT, EXPECT FULL YEAR 2020 AUCTION VALUES TO BE DOWN MORE THAN THE 5% THAT CO FORECASTED IN FEBRUARY - PRESENTATION.FORD MOTOR SAYS FOR FORD CREDIT, EXPECT NET RECEIVABLES TO DECLINE FURTHER - PRESENTATION.FORD MOTOR CO - FOR FORD CREDIT, LOWER EXPECTED ORIGINATIONS ARE PROJECTED TO DECREASE SIZE OF THE BALANCE SHEET AND FUNDING REQUIREMENTS IN 2020.FORD MOTOR CO - FOR FORD CREDIT, EXPECT TO INCREASE ABS MIX AND PRUDENTLY ISSUE UNSECURED DEBT.FORD MOTOR CO - FOR FORD CREDIT, EXPECT TO MAINTAIN LIQUIDITY AROUND TARGET LEVEL FOR THE REST OF THE YEAR.FORD MOTOR CO - FOR FORD CREDIT, WAIVED $3 BILLION ALLOCATION TO CORPORATE REVOLVER IN MARCH.'}{'symbol': 'F', 'date': '2020-04-29 18:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Ford Motor Reports Q1 Loss Of $0.50 Per Share', 'text': "QUARTERLY LOSS PER SHARE 50 CENTS.QUARTERLY ADJUSTED LOSS PER SHARE 23 CENTS.QUARTERLY REVENUE $34.32 BILLION VERSUS $40.34 BILLION.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $-0.12, REVENUE VIEW $32.34 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.EXPECTS SECOND-QUARTER ADJUSTED EBIT TO BE A LOSS OF MORE THAN $5 BILLION.QUARTERLY AUTOMOTIVE REVENUE $31.34 BILLION VERSUS $37.24 BILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.FIRST-QUARTER ADJUSTED FREE CASH FLOW WAS NEGATIVE $2.2 BILLION.SAYS RECORDED VOLUME-DRIVEN AUTOMOTIVE EBIT LOSS OF $177 MILLION IN QUARTER.SAYS STRONG FORD CREDIT PORTFOLIO PERFORMANCE IN QUARTER WAS OFFSET BY ABOUT $600 MILLION FROM INCREASED CREDIT-LOSS RESERVES, SOME HIGHER DEPRECIATION.SAYS BELIEVE THE COMPANY'S CASH IS SUFFICIENT TO TAKE CO THROUGH THE END OF THE YEAR.SAYS AT THE END OF FIRST QUARTER, FORD AND FORD CREDIT HAD $35.1 BILLION AND $28.0 BILLION IN LIQUIDITY, RESPECTIVELY.SAYS FORD CREDIT DELIVERED $30 MILLION IN Q1 EARNINGS BEFORE TAXES, DOWN $771 MILLION.SAYS BELIEVE COMPANY'S CASH IS SUFFICIENT TO TAKE CO THROUGH END OF THE YEAR, EVEN WITH NO ADDITIONAL VEHICLE WHOLESALES OR FINANCING ACTIONS.SAYS WHILE FORD SHUT DOWN PLANTS IN MARCH, CASH USE HAS REMAINED HIGH BECAUSE PRODUCTION SUPPLIER PAYABLES ARE ABOUT 45 DAYS.SAYS CASH OUTFLOW WILL BE SUBSTANTIALLY LOWER AFTER EARLY MAY AS FORD PAYS DOWN PRODUCTION SUPPLIER PAYABLES.SAYS EXPECTS Q2 ADJUSTED EBIT TO BE A LOSS OF MORE THAN $5 BILLION, AS YEAR-OVER-YEAR INDUSTRY VOLUMES DECLINE SIGNIFICANTLY IN EVERY REGION."}{'symbol': 'GRMN', 'date': '2020-04-29 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Garmin Withdraws Fiscal 2020 Guidance', 'text': 'GARMIN REPORTS STRONG REVENUE AND OPERATING INCOME GROWTH FOR FIRST QUARTER 2020; WITHDRAWS FISCAL 2020 GUIDANCE DUE TO COVID-19 ECONOMIC UNCERTAINTY.QTRLY TOTAL REVENUE OF $856 MILLION.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $0.84, REVENUE VIEW $821.5 MILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.STRONG BALANCE SHEET WITH NO DEBT AND $2.6 BILLION OF CASH AND MARKETABLE SECURITIES.'}{'symbol': 'GD', 'date': '2020-04-29 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'General Dynamics Q1 Earnings Per Share $2.43', 'text': 'GENERAL DYNAMICS REPORTS FIRST-QUARTER 2020 RESULTS.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.43.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $2.57 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q1 REVENUE $8.75 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $9.23 BILLION.QTRLY BACKLOG OF $85.7 BILLION, UP 24% FROM YEAR-AGO QUARTER.GENERAL DYNAMICS - QTRL-END ESTIMATED POTENTIAL CONTRACT VALUE WAS $38.1 BILLION.GENERAL DYNAMICS - QUARTER-END ESTIMATED POTENTIAL CONTRACT VALUE WAS $38.1 BILLION.QTRLY OPERATING MARGIN 10.8% VERSUS 10.9%.'}{'symbol': 'GE', 'date': '2020-04-29 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'GE Reports Q1 Adjusted EPS Of $0.05', 'text': 'GE - COVID-19 CHALLENGED FIRST-QUARTER RESULTS.GE - QTRLY CONTINUING EPS (GAAP) OF $0.72.GE -  QTRLY TOTAL REVENUES (GAA